{"title":"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_-_ruler_(last_effort)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 - ruler (last effort)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Remark_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_Innovative_Minds_(Similar_to_Solution_1_above)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by Innovative Minds (Similar to Solution 1 above)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All of the rectangles in the figure below, which is drawn to scale, are similar to the enclosing rectangle. Each number represents the area of the rectangle. What is length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Screenshot_2024-11-08_2.08.49_PM.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/c3/Screenshot_2024-11-08_2.08.49_PM.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"563\" height=\"372\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fada6ff95f8cf1420e501b8f1b4aa0030154bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }4+4\\sqrt5\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }10\\sqrt2\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }5+5\\sqrt5\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }10\\sqrt[4]{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"543\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is similar to 2000 AIME I Q4.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, let its short side be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the long side be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Observe that for every rectangle, since ratios of the side length of the rectangles are directly proportional to the ratios of the square roots of the areas (For example, each side of the rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dcba07bde5741ce967fc1b96296720f986e6375.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{9}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> times that of the rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), as they are all similar to each other.\n</p><p>The side opposite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> on the large rectangle is hence written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975a6db88e0dcdc0125b0de5c5b0e566b72bbc2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x + 4x + 2y\\sqrt{2} + 3y\\sqrt{2} = 10x+5y\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"311\" height=\"23\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7edea0e25f383bdea8054d6a2071d5957ae774dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y\\sqrt{2}+5x+7x = 4y\\sqrt{2}+12x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"23\" />. Since the two lengths are equal, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b422ff82fc28c3a662ca58f3a61e4d7f930db04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10x+5y\\sqrt{2} = 4y\\sqrt{2}+12x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"213\" height=\"23\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e6d722fb5a9f01b0ca862a9813bf24571846ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\sqrt{2} = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"23\" />. Therefore, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/e/99e6a129e571a738fc34cc4869417c75d7906d28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa22a3b6fdd8321ce93427ac874f16557593d663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d635a5ca07e149e3f5b48e62e6648879260e1187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x\\sqrt{2})(x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"24\" />, which we can evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f782abc4ce6d469063f7f3e3fec359411daca3e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"65\" height=\"43\" />. From this, we can plug back in to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa22a3b6fdd8321ce93427ac874f16557593d663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccf6318bd19a375ddd42202ab59ce80c2d2c000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sqrt[4]{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"23\" />. Substituting into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f12d6396cd9b4fb592b8e3f888d02b5d7cd9a0a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 4y\\sqrt{2}+12x = 4(\\sqrt[4]{2})(\\sqrt{2})+\\frac{12}{\\sqrt[4]{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"310\" height=\"43\" /> which can be evaluated to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e4021ab0e1e65adb3cd0c843ca0c66498cdefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }10\\sqrt[4]{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~i_am_suk_at_math_2\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that the area is an integer, so after finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/e/99e6a129e571a738fc34cc4869417c75d7906d28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"23\" />, AB must contain a 4th root. The only such option is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e4021ab0e1e65adb3cd0c843ca0c66498cdefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }10\\sqrt[4]{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the rectangle's height be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090565eab5a504dcb8e9345374e3f58777592c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> The entire rectangle has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6a0c2f300ca8335e5b945617a0faed2a1ad5cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> We will be using this fact for ratios.\n</p><p>Note that the short side of the rectangle with area 32 will have a height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/5/d75e3cce53446dc2576625d5e5d52b9d2bbb995c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{32}{200}}\\cdot x = \\frac{2}{5}x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"127\" height=\"45\" /> We use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> because it is apparent that the height of the rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is the shorter side, corresponding with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, the long side of the rectangle with area 36 has a height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff953259995435b8b4784c7c530a331e2c05b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{36}{200}}\\cdot y = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{10}y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"150\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Noting that the total height of the big rectangle has height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> we have the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/893bdfef14ec7040af6a82ef6df027aa7c0f85a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac25 x + \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{10}y = x \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"225\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Since the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fd20f4b9824ee46f3d35db9aca43ce02568c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=\\frac{y^2}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"74\" height=\"45\" /> is equal to 200, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4ab4d919b8f2c48d5fbb73234974cad6a7b08a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} y&amp;=\\sqrt{200\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ &amp;=\\sqrt{100\\sqrt{8}} \\\\ &amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }10\\sqrt[4]{8}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"127\" height=\"111\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_-_ruler_.28last_effort.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_-_ruler_(last_effort)\">Solution 3 - ruler (last effort)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 - ruler (last effort)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that the diagram is drawn to scale, we can use a ruler to estimate the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We start by measuring the lengths of the rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which may vary per viewing medium. For the sake of the solution, we use side lengths ~<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e89248d99363665753d499130fbe0f11793602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> cm and ~<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b8722a423c09cc333298318a89ce22d2bf90d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> cm. \n</p><p>To get the scale ratio from centimeters to the units in the problem, we need to find a ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/318f46ecdae4bc341a943123c0429720332a6c26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7x}{10}\\cdot\\frac{5x}{10}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>Solving this equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c56f6fcb2aea464ed91d0fc93cdcfe08bf0eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{35}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>We then measure the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />(will vary), to get ~<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/5919325081d4c1617a977b36202fa8f35aa69de2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10.2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> cm. We multiply this length by our early ratio to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/660bd2ecc8c61f61d344eeb1375bdf4bbefb843d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10 \\cdot 10.2}{\\sqrt{35}} = \\frac{102}{\\sqrt{35}} \\approx \\frac{102}{6} \\approx 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The answer choice closest to this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f9a9cc3045c6e5aa36f00d19a7cee67dfd87360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt[4]{8}\\approx16.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"21\" />, so therefore the closest answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e4021ab0e1e65adb3cd0c843ca0c66498cdefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }10\\sqrt[4]{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~shreyan.chethan\n</p><p>Note:\nNever ever use this in an actual test unless you're giving it a last ditch attempt.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark_2\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The specific numbers used in the solution above vary per test medium, but the method should still work.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote the short side of rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the long side of said rectangle to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46eb9db06bf3cd52f6ac6a55f1f7ad95b889829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"46\" height=\"40\" />. Since we're given that all the rectangles in the figure are similar, we can mark the long side of the rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/9646d16830dd8fa7a36dd566ac6ab17d3a559b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{18}y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"23\" /> and the short side of the rectangle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d8dd5f375b5f3874868d24a8820fe854a68a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d30a6d320ca547f65faf8114b1aba98ecd363e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+\\sqrt{18}y=7x \\to \\sqrt{18}y=6x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"23\" />. Using the aforementioned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46eb9db06bf3cd52f6ac6a55f1f7ad95b889829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"46\" height=\"40\" />, this equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f27d15b22cc81a97baecdf5d63a016f888a9643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{18}y=6 \\times \\frac{1}{y} \\to \\sqrt{18} y^2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"226\" height=\"42\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccf6318bd19a375ddd42202ab59ce80c2d2c000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sqrt[4]{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"23\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f782abc4ce6d469063f7f3e3fec359411daca3e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"65\" height=\"43\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e5d42428aad675d5d135d0ba0de0b725f2712c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB = \\sqrt{32}y+5x+7x = \\left(\\sqrt{32} \\times \\sqrt[4]{2}\\right) + \\left(12 \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\right) = 2^{\\frac{5}{2}} \\times 2^{\\frac{1}{4}} + \\frac{12}{2^{\\frac{1}{4}}}=\\frac{20}{2^{\\frac{1}{4}}}=\\frac{20 \\times 2^{\\frac{3}{4}}}{2}=\\frac{20 \\sqrt[4]{8}}{2}= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }10\\sqrt[4]{8}}\\]\" width=\"834\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~pandapower24\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fW7OGWee31c?si=oq7toGPh2QaksLHE\">https://youtu.be/fW7OGWee31c?si=oq7toGPh2QaksLHE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution 2 by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/8abGnAJZ3AM\">https://youtu.be/8abGnAJZ3AM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_Innovative_Minds_.28Similar_to_Solution_1_above.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_Innovative_Minds_(Similar_to_Solution_1_above)\">Video Solution 3 by Innovative Minds (Similar to Solution 1 above)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by Innovative Minds (Similar to Solution 1 above)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/EepOGN0_Rgw\">https://youtu.be/EepOGN0_Rgw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x_Nux5ufe-k?si=shgvzOEWZ_KhEqUX\">https://youtu.be/x_Nux5ufe-k?si=shgvzOEWZ_KhEqUX</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=3068s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=3068s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See 